  "master_record": "results/stage2/s50-invalidation-20261117T205855Z.json",
  "reason": "Adam8bit stored the second moment as a per-256-element linear absmax int8 code. Any squared gradient below about absmax/254 rounded to zero, and Adam then divided by eps whenever the current gradient was also small. The reproduction measures 57.7% of elements with a zeroed stored second moment and a nonzero first moment, a maximum update 3.2e4 times fp32 AdamW's, and a 313% parameter error after 50 steps. Every number produced by these runs is therefore a property of the defective optimiser; the learning-rate sweep reduced the damage but did not remove it, and the selected 3e-5 rate is not used. Receipts and checkpoints are retained verbatim and may not be used as a bar, baseline or selection input.",
  "revision": "547953f4d1a75f3d0cdc1d93d76d54a618d70929",
